<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; Creation and Providence" cic="CCC 279-324" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>What does it mean that God created the world &laquo;out of nothing&raquo; (creatio ex nihilo)? What does this imply for our understanding of God?</li>
<li>How do the three Persons of the Trinity participate in the work of creation?</li>
<li>What did God declare about his creation in Genesis 1:31? Why is this statement important?</li>
<li>What is divine providence and how does it relate to human freedom?</li>
<li>According to the Catechism, why does God permit evil? What supreme example does he give us?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. Think of something beautiful you have seen today &mdash; a tree, a cloud, someone&rsquo;s face. How does it change the way you see it knowing that God created it out of love and sustains it at this very moment?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Don&rsquo;t think of something distant. Look at what is close to you. Creation is not only the stars; it is also what is right in front of you.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. If creation is the work of the Trinity &mdash; Father, Son, and Holy Spirit &mdash; how does that change the way you relate to the material world?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Do you see the world as something &laquo;neutral&raquo; or as something that bears the mark of God&rsquo;s love?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. Do you find it hard to believe that the material world is &laquo;very good&raquo; (Gen 1:31)? Why or why not?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Sometimes we think that the spiritual is good and the material is bad. Where does that idea come from?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. How do you reconcile God&rsquo;s providence with the suffering you see around you? What does the cross say to you about this?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Don&rsquo;t look for a perfect answer. Write what you feel, what is difficult, what you hope for.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. Look around you right now. Can you see something that reminds you that God loves you and sustains your existence at this moment?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Name something concrete. Faith is lived in the details.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Creation Walk</h4>
<p>Go for a 10-minute walk. With each step, name aloud something God created: the sky, the plants, the air, the birds, the people. When you return, write a brief prayer of thanksgiving.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Reading Jeremiah 10:12-13</h4>
<p>Read the passage slowly, underlining God&rsquo;s actions: &laquo;made,&raquo; &laquo;established,&raquo; &laquo;stretched out,&raquo; &laquo;brings up,&raquo; &laquo;produces.&raquo; What does this poem tell you about God&rsquo;s power and tenderness?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Letter to the Creator</h4>
<p>Write a letter to God starting with &laquo;Thank you for creating me...&raquo; Tell him what you admire about creation, what is hard to understand, and what you want to entrust to him.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
